{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/62013-the-authorities-angelic-endgames-and-tactics","id":62013,"title":"The Authorities : Angelic Endgames and Tactics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-30T23:15:05-08:00","id":62013,"title":"The Authorities : Angelic Endgames and Tactics","content":"So, I'm running the angels lately, and I have a few questions!<br /> <br /> Do the angels have any real incentives they can offer Demons to 'flip'? This would be a useful story tool for me. Do they 'bribe' certain Demons with 'get out of jail free' cards, or even free passes for a certain amount of time? Our own federal government had to create the witness protection program to break the mafia. Otherwise, they couldn't gain the cooperation of valuable informants. Have Angels seen the virtue of this? Do they have like, a town somewhere where they can relocate 'authorized' Unchained that have 'gone state'?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the 'quotations marks!' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Secondly, what... in specific... HAPPENS to Unchained, when they get caught? Are they killed and recycled immediately? Or is there some sort of holding facility? I far prefer the latter for story purposes, but how to justify it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T00:14:43-08:00","id":62032,"title":"","content":"There's an angel in the book whose job is to entice demons back into the loving embrace of the G-M (or her loving embrace, whatever, no judgment) 219 ish I believe.<br /> There's also that guy from the matrix to consider.<br /> <br /> The book talks about Compromised Agencies around page 58.<br /> I believe this is what most demons are afraid of as it also discusses integrators setting up compromised agencies to offer up to the G-M.<br /> I believe 219 and 58 are your two best references for organized efforts to lure demons back to the G-M.<br /> 58 suggests that most demons in the compromised agency are there unwillingly, though I suppose there's no reason that willing demons in a kind of witness protection or re-education program are put to work in these agencies.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what exactly happens to a demon when captured.<br /> The fiction in between chapter 2 and 3 depicts an attempted interrogation between an angel and.. I think what was supposed to be a stigmatic human. I actually really like that piece of fiction. <br /> <br /> So it is possible that the demon could be held at a facility facing interrogation or reprogramming. Or perhaps the demon is held in a facility while recycling/reprograming/repair facilities are being prepared. OR perhaps it's a trap and the Demon is held in a facility awaiting rescue so all parties involved can be dealt with... maybe the demon is supposed to be rescued and re-integrated as some kind of sleeper.<br /> <br /> Really, what happens after an unchained is caught is up to you though there is fiction which suggests that repair centres exist; interrogations take place; and reprogramming can occur. <br /> <br /> Thats all I've got so far might take another look tommorrow evening.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:32:26-08:00","id":62130,"title":"","content":"The fiction bit I'm fairly sure was a demon, as the human succeeded in selling his face to the opposition. He was stalling long enough for a raid. And he was pretty obvious about stalling - thus the comment about the clueless angel not getting humans and recognizing suspicious behavior.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, what can an angel offer a demon? Naturally, there's fear and desire to play up. Fear - &quot;I don't want to be recycled and lose my individuality. If I help you get other demons, I get to live?&quot; Traitors in the midst trying to stay alive by selling out their fellows.<br /> <br /> The god machine doesn't like demons because they mess up its plans. They're the wrench thrown into its perfect calculations simply by merely existing. So, its trying to find some way to bring the rogue variables back into the fold; don't go automatically for the &quot;we will recycle you&quot; route, but instead offer other kinds of incentives to work -with- the God Machine. Even offer autonomy within a free jacked-in Cover. Do the mission, you get to continue your freedom.<br /> <br /> Integrators could be offered chances of redemption, or even covers they can jack-in to; many of them desire a half-state of being jacked in, but having autonomy. And, in truth, a demon is probably a better operative than angels in a lot of cases for the God Machine, so it could string along an Integrator for a long time as a resource in its plans.<br /> <br /> Tempters tend to be hedonistic, so they could be offered riches and pleasure that only the God Machine can offer. And its not like the God Machine doesn't make angels of temptation itself. Angle for win-win situations.<br /> <br /> Inquisitors can trade for information; they're info junkies after all. Insights into the state of the world that a mere demon cannot grasp on its own.<br /> <br /> Saboteurs... saboteurs are soldiers fighting for a cause - angels would have to undermine the saboteur's faith in the evil of the God Machine. Which isn't hard - the G.M. has built angels to stop astroids from hitting the earth. It encourages humans to develop scientific advancements - maybe for itself, but the benefits of computers and penicillin can't be denied. And the idea that, should the God Machine go down, there are hungry, eager, and frankly darker things that are more than willing to jump into the power vacuum that the God Machine protects against. The god machine wants to cultivate humans, at least, not destroy them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I suggest watching Burn Notice. At the very beginning of the series, it begins with a line. Something like, &quot;As a spy, you get used to doing bad things for good reasons. And to a spy, two wrongs do equal a right.&quot; Demons deal with criminals and drug dealers and thieves in their battle, even when those people are the ones who hurt others. Every demon has their own morality and reasons for falling, and yet still do bad things for sake of that reason. If the demon wants to protect people... then give the demon information about a project that, long term, will lead to health and survival of a large group of humans, and foiling the plan will lead to the deaths of many in a city.<br /> <br /> That's what happened to Michael. The organization that burned him actually recruited him by showing him what their plan was to save large amounts of people. and put an end to an evil force. The God Machine isn't evil. Its amoral, distant, and desires absolute order. But its existence is tied to humanity's, and will likely do anything in its power to protect humanity as a whole. Its goals may very well involve the greater good- which you can see given the information that neither demons nor angels have access to. It does bad things for the sake of the greater good - the same the demons are doing, but on a larger scale they cannot comprehend.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing to do is to make the demons and angels act as two sides of the same coin. Show that they want order, yes. Yet show they care for their charges. Show how they enjoy life as much as a demon does. The just have their orders, while demons are rebel. The God Machine tries to fit the best angel to the best job. So, personality wise, the angels fit their missions. They like their jobs. And they're good at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":".  Added more stuff! 01-31-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}